# OmniFlow QA — Build Prompt

**Tagline:** *Browse. Inspect. Automate. Heal.*

---

## 1. Project Overview

OmniFlow QA is a Chromium-engine–based automation browser purpose-built for QA Engineers, SDETs, and Automation Developers.

The browser must combine traditional browsing with deeply embedded automation tooling, enabling users to:

* Inspect elements intelligently
* Generate robust locators
* Record automation scripts
* Auto-heal broken selectors
* Replay recorded tests
* Produce rich execution reports
* Perform scraping and DOM extraction tasks

This browser is not a plugin — automation capabilities must be **native to the browser experience**.

---

## 2. Core Architecture

**Engine Base:**

* Chromium (latest stable fork)
* Maintain compatibility with Chrome DevTools Protocol (CDP)

**Language Stack:**

* C++ / Chromium base modifications
* Node.js bridge layer
* TypeScript automation APIs
* Python optional bindings (future)
* WebAssembly modules for performance tooling if needed

**Extension Layer:**

* Built-in DevTools panel
* Automation overlay UI
* Locator visualization layer

---

## 3. Core Feature Pillars

---

### 3.1 Smart Element Inspection

Enhanced DevTools inspector with automation context.

**Capabilities:**

* Hover to highlight elements
* DOM path visualization
* Shadow DOM traversal
* iFrame detection
* Dynamic element tracking
* Visibility & interactability scoring

**Locator generation must support:**

* id
* name
* class
* css selector
* xpath
* aria labels
* data-test attributes
* custom attributes
* text selectors
* relative locators
* shadow DOM selectors

Each locator must include:

* Stability score
* Uniqueness score
* Healing fallback ranking

---

### 3.2 Locator Auto-Healing Engine

AI + rules-based locator repair system.

**Functions:**

* Detect broken locators during replay
* Re-scan DOM for closest matches
* Compare attributes, structure, and text
* Use similarity scoring
* Replace locator dynamically
* Log healing events

**Healing strategies:**

* Attribute similarity
* DOM hierarchy comparison
* Visual position matching
* Text proximity
* AI pattern learning

---

### 3.3 Script Recorder

Record user browser interactions and convert them into executable automation scripts.

**Recordable actions:**

* Clicks
* Inputs / typing
* Dropdown selections
* Drag & drop
* File uploads
* Navigation
* Assertions
* Wait conditions
* Hover events
* Keyboard shortcuts

**Recording modes:**

* Manual start/stop
* Auto-record session
* Step recording

---

### 3.4 Script Export & File Saving

Recorded scripts must be exportable as files.

**Supported formats (MVP):**

* Selenium (Java, Python, JS)
* Playwright
* Cypress
* Puppeteer
* Raw CDP scripts

**File handling:**

* Save locally
* Version scripts
* Edit before export
* Add test data

---

### 3.5 Script Replay Engine

Replay recorded scripts inside the browser or headless.

**Capabilities:**

* Step execution
* Pause/resume
* Breakpoints
* Speed control
* Environment switching
* Parallel replay (future)

---

### 3.6 Reporting Engine

Reporting is a core pillar — not an add-on.

**Report types:**

* Execution summary
* Step pass/fail
* Screenshots per step
* Video recording
* Healed locator logs
* Performance timings
* Network logs

**Export formats:**

* HTML
* PDF
* JSON
* JUnit XML

**Dashboard:**

* Test history
* Failure trends
* Healing frequency
* Locator stability analytics

